    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d137-a2">

                <pb facs="0334" n="238" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg238"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure A in Mr. Bee’s letter.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bee to Mr.
                            Higby.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Francisco</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-06-11"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 11,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am requested by the proprietors of the
                    Roscoe cigar factory to present the following two Chinese mercantile firms—Kim,
                    Lung &amp; Co., 728 Dupont street, corner of Clay, and Quang Man, Long &amp;
                    Co., 620 Dupont street—both old firms in good standing financially, for your
                    acceptance of them for bondsmen in the sum of 5,000, either of which firms can
                    justify before you in the sum required on personal property security. Will you
                    oblige me by an early answer?</p>
                <p>Your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>F. A. BEE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">His Imperial Chinese
                            Majesty’s Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
